+## A citation must resolve (2026-10-26, check gains the citation check)
+
+**The rule, as it appears in `CLAUDE.md`:** *An INTERNALS citation must resolve. `check`
+matches each cited name against the `##` headings of `docs/INTERNALS.md` and names every
+citation with no matching heading as a gap.*
+
+**What happened.** The invariant "every rule in `CLAUDE.md` has an entry in
+`docs/INTERNALS.md`" sits in the hard invariants of `plan.md` section 5, and this file
+says a rule with no entry here is a draft. But nothing enforced it: `check` never read
+`docs/INTERNALS.md` at all. A citation could point at an entry that does not exist and
+the build stayed green - the citation was documentation, not a gate.
+
+**What was measured.** The repo's own `CLAUDE.md` carried nine live citations when this
+was built; all nine resolved, and resolving them required exactly what the check does:
+case-insensitive comparison against the heading's leading text, because two of the nine
+differ from their headings in case; the heading's `(date, reason)` suffix stripped,
+because no citation repeats it; and the cited name folded back to one line, because one
+citation wraps across two lines.
+
+**What is deliberately NOT done, and why.** Three misses, each decided:
+
+- A citation inside an HTML comment is skipped. The shipped template's `CLAUDE.md`
+  carries a commented-out example citation naming an entry that never exists; a check
+  that reads comments would be red in every correctly initialised project.
+- A missing `docs/INTERNALS.md` is not a citation gap. The structure audit already
+  reports the missing file; naming the same gap twice makes the report unreadable.
+- Only the full quoted pointer form counts as a citation. Prose that mentions the
+  pointer without the full form is documentation about the check, not a rule - the
+  identifier-only placeholder rule in use here, third time the same discipline: a check
+  that fires on correct documentation is a check that gets ignored.
+
+**Reopen trigger.** The citation form changes, or a project keeps its rules somewhere
+other than `CLAUDE.md`.
